# gitleaks fingerprint ignores.
#
# Prefer an allowlist entry in .gitleaks.toml over a line here: an allowlist
# says WHY, and is pinned by value and path. A fingerprint here is opaque and
# silently survives the string changing.
#
# Use this file only for a historical commit that cannot be rewritten -- the
# fingerprint form is `<commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>`.
#
# Current findings are handled by allowlists in .gitleaks.toml (see sections 1
# and 2 there). This file is intentionally empty.
